  "summary": "With --json, the tool outputs a JSON object containing prompt, directory_name, token_count, model_info, and files fields. The project ships an MCP server (code2prompt-mcp) that exposes codebase context generation to LLM applications like Claude Desktop, Cursor, Roo Code, and Cline, configured via an mcpServers JSON entry.",
